{"availability":"available","full":"AI-SDC/ACRO-R","name":"ACRO-R","description":"ACRO R Package: Tools for the Semi-Automatic Checking of Research Outputs. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"R","stars":4,"forks":2,"created":"2023-10-27T12:28:08Z","updated":"2026-10-05T17:48:14Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["data-privacy","data-protection","privacy","privacy-tools","statistical-disclosure-control","statistical-software"],"demo":"https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/AI-SDC/ACRO-R/main?urlpath=rstudio","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.438Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.438Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.438Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.438Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:41.313Z","stars":4,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","stars":4,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.438Z","stars":4,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repository maintains the ACRO R package, which is an interface to the Python ACRO package.","ACRO is a free and open source tool that supports the semi-automated checking of research outputs (SACRO) for privacy disclosure within secure data environments. SACRO is a framework that applies best-practice principles-based statistical disclosure control (SDC) techniques on-the-fly as researchers conduct their analysis. SACRO is designed to assist human checkers rather than seeking to replace them as with current automated rules-based approaches.","The ACRO package is a lightweight Python tool that sits over well-known analysis tools that produce outputs such as tables, plots, and statistical models. This package adds functionality to:"],"features":["automatically identify potentially disclosive outputs against a range of commonly used disclosure tests;","apply optional disclosure mitigation strategies as requested;","report reasons for applying SDC;","and produce simple summary documents trusted research environment staff can use to streamline their workflow and maintain auditable records."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO-R/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a8acfea52aed49ab4c387580bb417cf8faeccb908567a782e0e10015691f2c65","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:51.000Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.626Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T17:48:14Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This repository maintains the ACRO R package, which is an interface to the Python ACRO package.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO-R/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a8acfea52aed49ab4c387580bb417cf8faeccb908567a782e0e10015691f2c65","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO-R/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.626Z"},"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:59.455Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AI-SDC/ACRO-R/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T18:33:01.626Z","hash":"a8acfea52aed49ab4c387580bb417cf8faeccb908567a782e0e10015691f2c65","originalBytes":4248,"storedBytes":4248,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["acro","research","package","outputs","sacro","data","disclosure","python","sdc","checking","interface","checkers","cran","documentation","framework","grant","human","installation","mitigation","number","online","phase","principles-based","produce","rather","requested","researchers","see","semi-automatic","statistical","such","supports","their","them","tool","tools","try","using","about","accessible","acknowledgement","additional","additionally","adds","administrative","adr","after","against","analysis","analysis.","analytics","any","applies","apply","applying","approaches.","assist","auditable","automated","automatically","back-end.","before","best-practice","bottom-right","change","check","checkers.","checks","code","codecov","commonly","communication","components.","conduct","contains","control","core","creates","curren